## Frequently Asked Questions

### What is the cheapest 1ct diamond at Blue Nile?
As of July 2026, the cheapest GIA-certified 1ct natural round diamond at Blue Nile is a G-VS2 Excellent at [$3,230](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29090690?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Lab-grown 1ct rounds start considerably lower — under $1,000 for many grades.

### Is G-VS2 a good grade for a 1ct diamond?
Yes. G is near-colorless — the difference from D, E, or F is not visible in a normal setting environment. VS2 means inclusions are not visible to the naked eye. This combination is what most GIA-certified gemologists recommend as the optimal value grade for round brilliants.

### How much cheaper is princess cut vs round at Blue Nile?
For the same color and clarity, princess cut is approximately 25–35% cheaper than round brilliant at Blue Nile. A G-VS2 round starts at $3,230; a G-VS2 princess Ideal starts at $2,212 — that's about a $1,000 difference for the same grade.

### Should I buy the 0.90ct instead of 1ct?
If budget is a consideration, yes. The size difference between 0.90ct and 1.00ct is under 0.5mm in diameter — less than the width of a human hair. Most people cannot identify which is which when both rings are side by side.

The 0.90ct G-VS1 at $2,487 is a sharply better value than a 1.00ct G-VS2 at $3,230.

### Are Blue Nile lab-grown diamonds GIA certified?
Blue Nile sells lab-grown diamonds with both IGI and GIA certification. GIA-lab-grown diamonds at Blue Nile are typically priced slightly higher than IGI equivalents but carry more universal recognition. Both are legitimate certifications for lab-grown stones.

### Is Blue Nile's return policy good enough for a diamond purchase?
Yes. Blue Nile offers 30-day free returns with a prepaid label. This is sufficient to receive the diamond, have it independently appraised or inspected, and return it if the quality does not match what the certificate states. It is one of the better return windows among major online diamond retailers.

### Does fancy shape save money at Blue Nile?
Yes. For the same grade, oval, cushion, and emerald cuts are meaningfully cheaper than round at Blue Nile — typically 20–40% less per carat. Oval also has a larger face-up surface area than round for the same carat weight, which can make the ring look larger.

### What is the best clarity grade for a 1ct round on Blue Nile?
VS2 is the recommended minimum. At 1ct, VS2 inclusions are not visible to the naked eye — you need 10× magnification to see them. Spending more for VS1, VVS2, or VVS1 at 1ct produces no visible difference in normal wear and viewing.

The savings from VS2 vs VS1 ($200–$400 at this size) are better directed toward color or cut quality.

### Does Blue Nile offer financing for 1ct diamond purchases?
Yes. Blue Nile offers financing through Affirm with multiple term options (6, 12, or 24 months). A 1ct G-VS2 round at $3,230 financed over 12 months is approximately $270/month at qualifying rates.

Financing terms depend on credit approval. Blue Nile also accepts all major credit cards — some buyers use a card with a sign-up bonus to offset $200–$500 of the purchase price.

### Can I see a 1ct diamond in person before buying from Blue Nile?
Blue Nile is primarily an online retailer with no retail showrooms. You cannot see the specific stone in person before purchase. However, the 360° HD video on Blue Nile shows the actual stone rotating, which is a better evaluation tool than most in-store lighting environments that are designed to maximize diamond appearance.

The 30-day return policy means you can receive the stone, evaluate it at home (or with an independent jeweler), and return it if it does not match your expectations.

### What is Blue Nile's return policy on 1ct diamonds?
Blue Nile accepts returns within 30 days of delivery with a prepaid shipping label. The diamond must be in its original, unmodified condition. Blue Nile does not accept returns on diamonds that have been set into rings purchased elsewhere.

If you set the diamond in a Blue Nile ring, a separate ring return policy applies. For loose diamond purchases, the 30-day window is standard and sufficient for independent appraisal.

### Is a 1ct G-VS2 GIA Excellent round the best choice for most buyers?
For most buyers who want a natural round: yes. G is the entry point to the near-colorless range — most people and most jewelers cannot see the color difference from D, E, or F without controlled grading conditions. VS2 is the point where inclusions become invisible to the naked eye.

Excellent cut maximizes light return and face-up appearance. This combination represents the best optical performance at the lowest price point before diminishing returns kick in.

